From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: every scale in FullPanel without black bars

What: in "Full screen including notch" (FullPanel) the guest gets the
panel's size rounded up to the next size that fits the scale it wants (a
few pixels more: 2944x1912 for 1.6 on the 13-inch Air's 2940x1912), and the
window shows it scaled onto the panel, filling it (the layer's resize
gravity; the pointer maps by width and height each). The guest says which
scale it wants ({"scale": s} on the display port, its display agent, from
Omarchy's own setting or the panel button just pressed); QEMU checks it
(1 to 4), keeps it in PINGOUIN_FULLPANEL_SCALE_FILE (the VM's folder, from the
app) and, in FullPanel, gives the guest the new size at once. The next start
reads the file, so the guest has the size that fits from its first frame.
qemu.log: "full panel: guest WxH on the WxH panel (the guest's scale S)".
Without a scale (automatic) or one whose sizes are too far apart: the
panel's own size, as before. Outside FullPanel nothing changes (the clean
size below a notch, a window).

Why: #355 (@brianmerchant): the whole panel fits few of Omarchy's scale
presets (the 13-inch Air: 1, 1.33, 2, 4), so 1.25 and 1.6 became 1.33 and
2 in FullPanel; cutting rows (PR #355's way) brought back the black band
that #346 removed.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's FullPanel).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-fullpanel-scale.sh (the sizes, and the
wiring in the patched ui/cocoa.m at build time). Applies after
pingouin-cocoa-fullpanel.patch and pingouin-cocoa-fullpanel-scale-logic.patch.

